{"status":"ok","message-type":"work-list","message-version":"1.0.0","message":{"facets":{},"total-results":3456365,"items":[{"indexed":{"date-parts":[[2026,8,11]],"date-time":"2026-08-11T17:46:16Z","timestamp":1786470376847,"version":"build-2736575974"},"posted":{"date-parts":[[2026]]},"reference-count":0,"publisher":"National Laboratory of the Rockies","content-domain":{"domain":[],"crossmark-restriction":false},"DOI":"10.66816\/pr3046335","type":"posted-content","created":{"date-parts":[[2026,8,11]],"date-time":"2026-08-11T17:18:31Z","timestamp":1786468711000},"source":"Crossref","is-referenced-by-count":0,"title":["Towards Scientific Foundation Models for Complex Energy Systems (Citation Only)"],"prefix":"10.66816","member":"12964","deposited":{"date-parts":[[2026,8,11]],"date-time":"2026-08-11T17:18:31Z","timestamp":1786468711000},"score":29.084316,"resource":{"primary":{"URL":"https:\/\/research-hub.nlr.gov\/en\/publications\/09191331-4a8e-4732-a379-e7d0da13fcbc"}},"issued":{"date-parts":[[2026]]},"references-count":0,"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.66816\/pr3046335","published":{"date-parts":[[2026]]},"subtype":"preprint"},{"indexed":{"date-parts":[[2026,10,5]],"date-time":"2026-10-05T14:05:50Z","timestamp":1791209150766,"version":"4.1.0"},"posted":{"date-parts":[[2026]]},"group-title":"SSRN","reference-count":0,"publisher":"Elsevier BV","license":[{"start":{"date-parts":[[2026,1,1]],"date-time":"2026-01-01T00:00:00Z","timestamp":1767225600000},"content-version":"unspecified","delay-in-days":0,"URL":"https:\/\/creativecommons.org\/licenses\/by-nc\/4.0\/"}],"content-domain":{"domain":[],"crossmark-restriction":false},"abstract":"<jats:p>This article gives a narrow, testable meaning to zero-latency coherence transport in Viscous Time Theory (VTT). The label does not assert zero experimental duration, a superluminal process, an instantaneous collapse law, or a modification of standard quantum mechanics. It denotes a formal noncontinuability statement: a continuously recoverable regime (M3) reaches a boundary at which no further continuous M3 interpolation is available, so a separately declared post-boundary regime (M4) must supply an explicit selection relation. The construction begins with the standard quantuminstrument baseline: a density operator evolves on M3 through a completely-positive-compatible normal form in a positive intrinsic coordinate, while a multimargin combines recoverability, the spectrum of a declared diagnostic Hessian, and clock regularity. At first exit, the M4 relation must agree with a valid quantum instrument whenever it represents a measurement outcome. Three results delimit the proposal. Positive intrinsic-clock density reparametrizes a continuous M3 path rather than establishing an absolute physical time. A nonselective trace-preserving local instrument leaves the remote marginal invariant, so the proposed selection relation cannot be used for signaling. Preboundary M3 information alone does not identify a unique M4 image. Synthetic normal forms distinguish a resolved finite record from an ideal endpoint relation and illustrate margin loss, without presenting empirical evidence. The framework preserves VTT's original ambition at the precise point where its quantum specialization must become operational: any added predictive content must be benchmarked against standard quantum filtering, constrained by complete positivity and nosignaling, and tested prospectively.<\/jats:p>","DOI":"10.2139\/ssrn.7554539","type":"posted-content","created":{"date-parts":[[2026,10,5]],"date-time":"2026-10-05T13:30:51Z","timestamp":1791207051000},"source":"Crossref","is-referenced-by-count":0,"title":["Zero-Latency Coherence Transport and Quantum Reconfiguration A Quantum-Measurement Boundary Framework for Viscous Time Theory"],"prefix":"10.2139","author":[{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0009-0001-4217-9438","authenticated-orcid":true,"given":"Raoul","family":"Bianchetti","sequence":"first","affiliation":[],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]}],"member":"78","deposited":{"date-parts":[[2026,10,5]],"date-time":"2026-10-05T13:30:51Z","timestamp":1791207051000},"score":27.02515,"resource":{"primary":{"URL":"https:\/\/www.ssrn.com\/abstract=7554539"}},"issued":{"date-parts":[[2026]]},"references-count":0,"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.2139\/ssrn.7554539","published":{"date-parts":[[2026]]},"subtype":"preprint"},{"indexed":{"date-parts":[[2026,4,21]],"date-time":"2026-04-21T02:39:46Z","timestamp":1776739186922,"version":"3.51.2"},"posted":{"date-parts":[[2026]]},"group-title":"SSRN","reference-count":0,"publisher":"Elsevier BV","content-domain":{"domain":[],"crossmark-restriction":false},"abstract":"<jats:p>Background: The rapid growth of biomedical literature has rendered traditional systematic reviews unsustainable. Although large language models (LLMs) offer automation potential, citation fabrication and unreliable evidence discrimination remain critical barriers in evidence-based medicine. This study aims to design an autonomous AI agent built on the PubMed E-utilities API capable of citation-faithful, zero-hallucination retrieval of evidence through natural-language queries.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Methods: PubChat was built on a model-agnostic LangChain framework with three modes (Broad, Standard, Core). It integrates five-level hierarchical decomposition, adaptive iterative retrieval, embedding pre-filtering, and three-stage LLM verification. Head-to-head retrieval performance was benchmarked against eight state-of-the-art LLMs and specialized literature retrieval tools using 585 articles from Cochrane systematic reviews across eight languages as ground truth. Evaluation metrics included precision, recall, F1-score, F2-score, normalized discounted cumulative gain (nDCG), and source fidelity. User evaluation included 279 biomedical researchers from 18 countries, assessing reliability, innovation, efficiency, user experience, and preference using 28 five-point Likert-scale items. Micro-Innovation Discovery Engine (MIDE) was developed as a standalone companion tool.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Findings: PubChat-Broad retrieved the highest number of articles per review (242.6\u202f\u00b1\u202f92.6), followed by Standard (179.5\u202f\u00b1\u202f81.0) and Elicit (120.3\u202f\u00b1\u202f45.4) (P\u202f&amp;lt;\u202f0.001). PubChat produced no fabricated citations in this benchmark. PubChat-Core achieved the highest precision (0.25\u202f\u00b1\u202f0.15), F1 (0.30\u202f\u00b1\u202f0.15), and F2 (0.37\u202f\u00b1\u202f0.17), while Broad and Standard led ranking quality (nDCG 0.44\u202f\u00b1\u202f0.17 and 0.43\u202f\u00b1\u202f0.16). All three PubChat modes significantly outperformed most competitor tools (Kruskal-Wallis H = 107.83, P &amp;lt; 0.001). In the user evaluation, satisfaction exceeded 80\/100, with clear preference over specialized tools (78%) and manual search (72%). MIDE further demonstrates PubChat\u2019s downstream utility by converting high-recall corpora into ten evidence-traceable research gaps linking periodontitis and chronic kidney disease.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Interpretation: PubChat is a scalable, user-friendly agent that integrates reliable evidence retrieval with structured literature synthesis to facilitate biomedical discovery.<\/jats:p>","DOI":"10.2139\/ssrn.6611963","type":"posted-content","created":{"date-parts":[[2026,4,21]],"date-time":"2026-04-21T01:47:01Z","timestamp":1776736021000},"source":"Crossref","is-referenced-by-count":0,"title":["PubChat: An Autonomous AI Agent for Zero Citation Hallucination, High-Recall PubMed Evidence Retrieval"],"prefix":"10.2139","author":[{"given":"Xuenan","family":"Zhuang","sequence":"first","affiliation":[],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]},{"given":"Dan","family":"Cao","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]},{"given":"Liang","family":"Zhang","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]},{"given":"See","family":"PDF","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]}],"member":"78","deposited":{"date-parts":[[2026,4,21]],"date-time":"2026-04-21T01:47:01Z","timestamp":1776736021000},"score":25.843813,"resource":{"primary":{"URL":"https:\/\/www.ssrn.com\/abstract=6611963"}},"issued":{"date-parts":[[2026]]},"references-count":0,"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.2139\/ssrn.6611963","published":{"date-parts":[[2026]]},"subtype":"preprint"},{"indexed":{"date-parts":[[2026,11,11]],"date-time":"2026-11-11T00:26:37Z","timestamp":1794356797221,"version":"4.9.0"},"edition-number":"1","reference-count":0,"publisher":"Wiley","isbn-type":[{"value":"9780470722398","type":"print"},{"value":"9780470718964","type":"electronic"}],"license":[{"start":{"date-parts":[[1956,1,1]],"date-time":"1956-01-01T00:00:00Z","timestamp":-441849600000},"content-version":"tdm","delay-in-days":0,"URL":"http:\/\/doi.wiley.com\/10.1002\/tdm_license_1.1"}],"content-domain":{"domain":[],"crossmark-restriction":false},"published-print":{"date-parts":[[1956,1]]},"DOI":"10.1002\/9780470718964.ch11","type":"other","created":{"date-parts":[[2008,5,30]],"date-time":"2008-05-30T04:56:12Z","timestamp":1212123372000},"page":"141-155","source":"Crossref","is-referenced-by-count":0,"title":["The Simulation of Telepathy"],"prefix":"10.1002","author":[{"given":"E. J.","family":"Dingwall","sequence":"first","affiliation":[],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]}],"member":"311","published-online":{"date-parts":[[2008,5,30]]},"container-title":["Novartis Foundation Symposia","Ciba Foundation Symposium \u2010 Extrasensory Perception"],"language":"en","link":[{"URL":"https:\/\/onlinelibrary.wiley.com\/doi\/pdf\/10.1002\/9780470718964.ch11","content-type":"unspecified","content-version":"vor","intended-application":"similarity-checking"}],"deposited":{"date-parts":[[2023,8,26]],"date-time":"2023-08-26T13:55:33Z","timestamp":1693058133000},"score":25.433178,"resource":{"primary":{"URL":"https:\/\/onlinelibrary.wiley.com\/doi\/10.1002\/9780470718964.ch11"}},"issued":{"date-parts":[[1956,1]]},"ISBN":["9780470722398","9780470718964"],"references-count":0,"alternative-id":["10.1002\/9780470718964.ch11","10.1002\/SERIES1767","10.1002\/9780470718964"],"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.1002\/9780470718964.ch11","archive":["Portico"],"relation":{"is-part-of":[{"id-type":"doi","id":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.1002\/9780470718964","asserted-by":"object"}]},"ISSN":["1935-4657"],"issn-type":[{"value":"1935-4657","type":"electronic"}],"published":{"date-parts":[[1956,1]]}},{"indexed":{"date-parts":[[2026,7,30]],"date-time":"2026-07-30T10:31:30Z","timestamp":1785407490764,"version":"3.56.0"},"reference-count":0,"publisher":"Research on Research Institute","content-domain":{"domain":[]},"published-print":{"date-parts":[[2026,6,27]]},"DOI":"10.70744\/metaror.356.2.ea","type":"peer-review","created":{"date-parts":[[2026,6,29]],"date-time":"2026-06-29T15:02:23Z","timestamp":1782745343000},"source":"Crossref","is-referenced-by-count":0,"title":["Editorial Assessment: Citation accuracy, citation noise, and citation bias: A foundation of citation analysis (Round 2)"],"prefix":"10.70744","member":"51568","review":{"type":"editor-report","running-number":"356.EA2","revision-round":"2","stage":"post-publication","competing-interest-statement":"No competing interests","language":"en"},"deposited":{"date-parts":[[2026,6,29]],"date-time":"2026-06-29T15:03:56Z","timestamp":1782745436000},"score":25.305847,"resource":{"primary":{"URL":"https:\/\/metaror.org\/article\/citation-accuracy-citation-noise-and-citation-bias-a-foundation-of-citation-analysis-2\/#toc_Editorial_assessment"}},"editor":[{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0000-0001-8249-1752","authenticated-orcid":true,"given":"Ludo","family":"Waltman","sequence":"first","affiliation":[{"id":[{"id":"https:\/\/ror.org\/027bh9e22","id-type":"ROR","asserted-by":"publisher"}]}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"editor"}]}],"issued":{"date-parts":[[2026,6,27]]},"references-count":0,"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.70744\/metaror.356.2.ea","relation":{"is-review-of":[{"id-type":"doi","id":"10.70744\/MetaROR.placeholder01","asserted-by":"subject"}]},"published":{"date-parts":[[2026,6,27]]}}],"items-per-page":5,"query":{"start-index":0,"search-terms":null}}}